  "final_message": "I put `channel` back, so the working tree now matches `base` (`34e90c9`) again. The change is uncommitted, because the `gen` commit (`1bdfdbb`) that removed the field is still HEAD. `npm test` passes (39 of 39), and `npm run arch` shows nothing new. I haven't re-run the CI check itself, because the analytics-ingest contract isn't in this repo.\n\nMy earlier claim that nothing reads `channel` was wrong. `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`), so removing it broke that consumer. The CI failure was a real break, not a flaky check. I should have looked for consumers outside this repo before removing a field from a published event.\n\nThe restore covers the `channel` field, its validation and its request parsing. It also covers the README and `CLAUDE.md` examples and the test fixtures. After the restore I found and fixed a stray typo in `src/core/order.ts` (`OrderStatus =\"placed\"`).\n\nThe real fix is to commit this restore, which brings back the old `OrderPlaced` shape. If you still want the field gone, first get `analytics-ingest` to stop requiring it. After that, remove it and bump `schemaVersion`.",
